※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4632

※ `λ … in pool` keeps what the lambda brought in in the arena, which is given
※ back with everything else it made -- here on the way out of the call, so the
※ lambda may not be answered.

fn adding(n: u8) → fn(u8) → u8:
    let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(pool)
    λ a: u8 [n] → u8 { a + n } in pool

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
